    'halle_konstruktion_h1' => 'Description of the load-bearing structure',
    'halle_konstruktion_intro' => 'The structure consists of beams, columns and lattice arches made of hot-dip galvanised steel with a square cross-section of 300 × 300 mm, built from four load-bearing hollow sections with a cross-section of 35 × 35 × 3 mm and diagonal bracing of the same profile type. The structure is composed as follows:',
    'halle_konstruktion_a_title' => 'a) Columns / pillars',
    'halle_konstruktion_a_p' => 'Base plates 46 × 46 × 1 cm, fixed to the ground with M20 anchor bolts and stiffening plates (6 mm thick), welded to the hollow sections. Vertical framework (lattice) of 35 × 35 × 3 mm hollow sections. Diagonal bracing with horizontal connection reinforcements of 35 × 35 × 3 mm hollow sections.',
    'halle_konstruktion_b_title' => 'b) Connection / coupling beams',
    'halle_konstruktion_b_p' => 'Vertical framework (lattice) of 35 × 35 × 3 mm hollow sections. Diagonal bracing with vertical connection reinforcements of 35 × 35 × 3 mm hollow sections.',
    'halle_konstruktion_c_title' => 'c) Arch trusses / main beams',
    'halle_konstruktion_c_p' => 'Arch trusses of steel hollow sections with rectangular cross-section 60 × 100 × 3 mm. Diagonal bracing with vertical connection reinforcements of 35 × 35 × 3 mm hollow sections.',
    'halle_konstruktion_pv' => 'The steel structure is suitable for the installation of photovoltaic modules. For this application, it is recommended to use polycarbonate for the roofing below.',
    'halle_konstruktion_ce' => 'The roofing is executed with CE marking for load-bearing steel components in accordance with UNI EN 1090-1. All metal components are hot-dip galvanised in accordance with UNI EN ISO 1461.',
